# Dashboard portal UI modernization

When refactoring **client** (`/dashboard`) or **admin** (`/dashboard/admin`) **UI only**, follow this spec. Full narrative lives in [public/admin-client-portals.mdc](mdc:public/admin-client-portals.mdc). **Do not** change APIs, auth, routes, env, or DB without an explicit request.

## Hard constraints

- Preserve behaviour: same Supabase queries, gateway calls, forms, and publish flows.
- No renames of endpoints, tables, or route paths.
- Prefer **incremental** layout/component extraction over rewriting `admin-dashboard-page.tsx` wholesale.

## Cohesion (do not contradict)

- [quote-first-client-admin-dashboards.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/quote-first-client-admin-dashboards.mdc) — one trip story; **three** client-facing services: **transfers**, **golf courses**, **hotels** (accommodation). Map “quick actions” to these plus **documents / proposals / messages**, not generic telecom (“devices”, “usage”) unless product expands.
- [admin-operations-dashboard.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/admin-operations-dashboard.mdc) — hero + jump anchors, forest / fairway / gold, `rounded-[2rem]`, `shadow-soft`, non-technical copy.

## Visual system (from existing brand)

- Colours: `gs.bg` (`#F4F7F5`), `gs.dark` (`#063B2A`) body copy on marketing, `gs.green`, `forest-*`, `gold-*`, `ge.teal` accents — see `tailwind.config.js` and `.ge-page` in `src/index.css`.
- Typography: marketing home uses `fontFamily.ge` (**Open Sans**); dashboard previews under `public/dashboard-ui-preview/` mirror that + crest `/golfsol-crest-brand.svg`.
- Components: layered **cards**, **soft shadows**, **2rem** rounding, subtle **gradients** on hero only; **glassmorphism** sparingly.
- Motion: **hover lift** on cards/buttons, **fade-in** on sections, **skeleton** loaders and **empty states** where data can be absent.

## Client dashboard — target layout blocks

1. **Hero header** — greeting + name; optional status chips (e.g. proposal ready); avatar + notification affordance; branded gradient / soft shape **behind** content (decorative).
2. **Primary overview card** — single “your trip” summary (latest enquiry / package), healthy status cues, primary CTAs (e.g. view proposal, message desk).
3. **Quick actions** — short grid: Transfers · Golf · Hotels · Support/docs; touch-friendly targets (min ~44px height).
4. **Secondary resource cards** — counts/badges for open interest threads, invoices, transfer rows; hover + shadow.
5. **Navigation** — responsive: **bottom bar** on small screens, **sidebar or top** pattern consistent with `DashboardLayout`; clear active state.

## Admin dashboard — target layout blocks

1. **Same design language** as client (not a separate “legacy admin” skin).
2. **KPI strip** — operational metrics staff care about (e.g. pending enquiries, pipeline stages) using cards, not dense tables above the fold.
3. **Queue mindset** — filters/search + scannable rows; charts/widgets **secondary** to actions.
4. **Activity / alerts** — compact feed or banner region for time-sensitive items.
5. **Dark mode** — if implemented, use CSS variables + `class` on root; keep contrast for forest/gold on dark surfaces.

## Implementation checklist

- [ ] Reuse or extend `DashboardLayout`, `AdminOperationsHubHero`, portal cards — avoid duplicate “design systems”.
- [ ] New sections: stable `id` + `scroll-mt-*` when sticky chrome exists.
- [ ] Loading: skeletons or existing shells — no layout jump.
- [ ] a11y: focus order, `aria-` on nav/toggles, visible focus rings.
- [ ] Preview static mocks before large merges: `public/dashboard-ui-preview/` (see `index.html`).

